stion-6aaad334-a3c0-5643-a528-243af5b47439" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-87ff2314-8fb7-54d5-87c5-d6b7e1e45b40"] [17592186096690 :knowledge-point/questions "question-6aaad334-a3c0-5643-a528-243af5b47439"] ["question-009a4381-6aca-5a6f-b010-2dbc7da60371" :question/id #uuid "009a4381-6aca-5a6f-b010-2dbc7da60371"] ["question-009a4381-6aca-5a6f-b010-2dbc7da60371" :question/math-academy-id "q-118921"] ["question-009a4381-6aca-5a6f-b010-2dbc7da60371" :question/problem "![](images/7b/7b676396ae24fe47c832e4442b67a9ba66128eff11a8c08f7570704c0a16eeb7.png)\n\nConsider the picture shown above. Find $|a+b|.$"] ["question-009a4381-6aca-5a6f-b010-2dbc7da60371" :question/worked-solution "We use the triangle law of addition for $a$ and $b.$ We can start $a$ from an arbitrary point on the plane. The resultant goes from the start of $a$ to the head of $b.$\n\n![](images/87/87a40729c97eddcba2820dc083002aad9ee4d05d7e9e654bcf51d8410a2e4861.png)\n\nNow, in $△AHB$ we have $∠AHB={90}^{∘}$, $AH=30\\,\\text{mm}$ and $BH=20\\,\\text{mm}.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b| & =AB \\\\  & =\\sqrt{A{H}^{2}+B{H}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{30}^{2}+{20}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1\\,300} \\\\  & =10\\sqrt{13}\\,\\text{mm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-009a4381-6aca-5a6f-b010-2dbc7da60371" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-17441dbe-6903-5e53-bc8a-41e64fe4b46d" :answer-field/id #uuid "17441dbe-6903-5e53-bc8a-41e64fe4b46d"] ["answer-1b371911-bbad-59a4-a192-de4fbe2c032e" :answer/id #uuid "1b371911-bbad-59a4-a192-de4fbe2c032e"] ["answer-1b371911-bbad-59a4-a192-de4fbe2c032e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1b371911-bbad-59a4-a192-de4fbe2c032e" :answer/value "10\\sqrt{13}\\,\\text{mm}"] ["answer-cd1104ea-933b-5ad2-b216-bcff58d29534" :answer/id #uuid "cd1104ea-933b-5ad2-b216-bcff58d29534"] ["answer-cd1104ea-933b-5ad2-b216-bcff58d29534" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-cd1104ea-933b-5ad2-b216-bcff58d29534" :answer/value "50\\,\\tex